gabq(){return"Training load of a ride"},
gabo(){return"How hard the whole ride felt, from 0 to 10, times its length in minutes. A 60-minute ride you rate 5 counts as 300 points."},
gabp(){return"It measures how hard the ride felt to you, not your power or heart rate. Rate the whole ride, not its hardest moment."},
gabd(){return"This week compared with your usual week"},
gabb(){return"Your training load over the last 7 days, divided by your average week over the 4 weeks before them."},
gabc(){return"Coaches often treat a week more than about one and a half times your usual week as a warning sign. That rule comes from team sports, and its link to injury is debated, so Ride Doctor only uses it to suggest an easier day."},
